Tree Node Depth Calculation in Binary Search Tree (BST)
1. Problem Statement
Write a C++ program to construct a Binary Search Tree (BST) by inserting a set of integer values. The program should calculate
and display the depth of every node in the tree. It should also accept a specific node value from the user, display the path 
from the root to that node, and calculate its depth. If the specified node is not present in the tree, the program should 
display an appropriate message.
